[WORK]
UID: WORK-SDOC-TREE-SITTER-GRAMMAR
TITLE: A tree-sitter grammar for the sdoc format, derived from the sdoc grammar
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A dedicated tree-sitter grammar for the sdoc file format itself, derived from
the sdoc .sgra grammar so the two stay in step rather than being maintained
as two independent descriptions of the same format.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Operator, 2026-09-02, verbatim: "sdoc grammars to custom tree-sitter grammar"

A patched upstream grammar already exists at
`overlays/generic/tree-sitter-strictdoc.nix` and its adjacent `.patch`,
consumed by `checks/strictdoc-grammar-corpus.nix`, which parses every
`.sdoc`/`.sgra` in this repository, and it was extended on 2026-09-03
(commit d6633588) to teach `file_entry` StrictDoc's full File relation key
set after element-grained relations stopped four documents parsing.
<<<
